//! What a table IS, without reading all of it.
//!
//! Asked "what does this spreadsheet say?", an agent with only `sheet_read` pulls thousands
//! of cells into context and spends most of them working out that column C holds dates. The
//! file can answer that about itself in a few hundred tokens, and the answer is what you
//! need to decide which columns are worth plotting.
//!
//! Deliberately NOT insight. This reports shape — types, fill, cardinality, ranges. What it
//! MEANS is a judgement, and judgement is the agent's job; handing it a confident summary
//! generated by a heuristic would give it something to repeat rather than something to
//! reason from.
//!
//! (Named `tableprofile` because `profile` is taken by the user-profile module.)

